    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "l4he8pa",
      "content": "Inflation refers to a sustained rise in the general price level of goods and services over a period of time. It reduces the purchasing power of money."
    },
    {
      "id": "41b0crb",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "1. TYPES OF INFLATION"
    },
    {
      "id": "ziu5t0b",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Type</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Explanation</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Demand-Pull Inflation</p>",
            "<p>Demand exceeds supply</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Cost-Push Inflation</p>",
            "<p>Rise in production costs</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Creeping Inflation</p>",
            "<p>Slow and steady rise</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Galloping Inflation</p>",
            "<p>Rapid price rise</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Hyperinflation</p>",
            "<p>Extremely high inflation</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "le9rtkl",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "2. CAUSES OF INFLATION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cjjcvg5",
      "content": "• Increase in money supply<br></br>• Excess demand<br></br>• Rising wages<br></br>• Increase in fuel prices<br></br>• Supply shocks<br></br>"
    },
    {
      "id": "uswkxs5",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "3. EFFECTS OF INFLATION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ovxvv1p",
      "content": "• Decreases purchasing power<br></br>• Affects fixed income groups<br></br>• Creates uncertainty<br></br>• Encourages speculation<br></br>"
    },
    {
      "id": "933g5q9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "4. CONTROL OF INFLATION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "etxkdtb",
      "content": "Monetary Measures:<br></br>• Increase Repo Rate<br></br>• Increase CRR &amp; SLR<br></br>• Sell government securities<br></br><br></br>Fiscal Measures:<br></br>• Reduce government expenditure<br></br>• Increase taxes<br></br>"
    },
    {
      "id": "j3rp2g7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "5. MEASUREMENT OF INFLATION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fy5i6hu",
      "content": "Inflation is measured through:<br></br>• Consumer Price Index (CPI)<br></br>• Wholesale Price Index (WPI)<br></br>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kw20s12",
      "content": "RBI targets CPI inflation (4% ± 2%)."
    },
    {
      "id": "e8y3oug",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "PART 2: BUSINESS CYCLE"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9kepdgb",
      "content": "Business Cycle refers to periodic fluctuations in economic activity."
    },
    {
      "id": "l2r188s",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "1. PHASES OF BUSINESS CYCLE"
    },
    {
      "id": "5q2l7rx",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Phase</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Characteristics</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Expansion</p>",
            "<p>Increase in output &amp; employment</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Peak</p>",
            "<p>Highest level of activity</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Recession</p>",
            "<p>Decline in output</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Depression</p>",
            "<p>Severe downturn</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "CHAPTER 7: INFLATION & BUSINESS CYCLE",
      "id": "xmif5kf"
    },
    {
      "id": "em10a43",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "2. CAUSES OF BUSINESS CYCLE"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ygbxkn0",
      "content": "• Changes in investment<br></br>• Credit expansion or contraction<br></br>• Technological changes<br></br>• External shocks<br></br>"
    },
    {
      "id": "m3iln3m",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "3. CONTROL OF BUSINESS CYCLE"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7v0m62y",
      "content": "During Recession:<br></br>• Lower interest rates<br></br>• Increase public spending<br></br><br></br>During Inflationary Boom:<br></br>• Raise interest rates<br></br>• Reduce money supply"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rqpoc1m",
      "content": "<strong>PART 3 : ADVANCED INFLATION CONCEPTS</strong>"
    },
    {
      "id": "41ge4qu",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "<strong>PHILLIPS CURVE</strong>"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "jge3r23",
      "type": "image",
      "imageId": "o2jspwv",
      "src": "/books/Precis/RRB COMPLETE GK/images/image_o2jspwv.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lhqd558",
      "content": "The Phillips Curve shows the inverse relationship between inflation and unemployment in the short run. When unemployment decreases, inflation tends to rise, and vice versa."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5bu3xss",
      "content": "Short-Run Phillips Curve:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "k1ct9le",
      "content": "• Downward sloping curve.<br></br>• Low unemployment → High inflation.<br></br>• High unemployment → Low inflation."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7cfk93r",
      "content": "Long-Run Phillips Curve:"
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Feature",
        "Headline Inflation",
        "Core Inflation"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Commodity Coverage",
          "Includes all goods and services, including food and fuel",
          "Excludes volatile items like food and energy products"
        ],
        [
          "Volatility Level",
          "High volatility due to supply shocks and seasonal factors",
          "Low volatility, reflecting underlying long-term economic trend"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "9b37dsh"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "23az7sl",
      "content": "• Vertical at Natural Rate of Unemployment.<br></br>• No long-term trade-off between inflation and unemployment."
    },
    {
      "id": "xji206r",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Run</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Relationship</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Short Run</p>",
            "<p>Inverse relationship</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Long Run</p>",
            "<p>No trade-off (Vertical curve)</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cln31n3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. STAGFLATION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4ulvjn8",
      "content": "Stagflation is a situation where the economy experiences high inflation, high unemployment, and low economic growth simultaneously."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "n66lbn7",
      "content": "It contradicts the traditional Phillips Curve concept."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "g6t2p53",
      "content": "Major Cause:<br></br>• Supply shocks (e.g., oil crisis of 1970s)<br></br>• Increase in production costs<br></br>"
    },
    {
      "id": "2xlvisl",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Indicator</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Condition in Stagflation</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Inflation</p>",
            "<p>High</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Unemployment</p>",
            "<p>High</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "75azkrj",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. CORE vs HEADLINE INFLATION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hqcgyhg",
      "content": "Headline Inflation includes all goods and services including food and fuel.<br></br>Core Inflation excludes volatile items like food and fuel."
    },
    {
      "id": "7ks1mg1",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Aspect</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Headline Inflation</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Core Inflation</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Includes</p>",
            "<p>All items</p>",
            "<p>Excludes food &amp; fuel</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Volatility</p>",
            "<p>Highly volatile</p>",
            "<p>More stable</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "v3a0ecd",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. DEMAND-SUPPLY GRAPH EXPLANATION OF INFLATION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xiojg24",
      "content": "Demand-Pull Inflation (Graph Explanation):"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Distinction between Core Inflation and Headline Inflation is frequently asked in competitive exams.",
        "Identification of specific phases and causes of the Business Cycle.",
        "Demand-Supply graph interpretations of inflation mechanisms and Stagflation definitions."
      ],
      "id": "77m3t4f"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ihrvpwk",
      "content": "• Initial equilibrium at intersection of AD and AS.<br></br>• Increase in Aggregate Demand shifts AD curve right.<br></br>• New equilibrium at higher price level.<br></br>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "l32ky7x",
      "content": "Cost-Push Inflation (Graph Explanation):"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7zz9s8t",
      "content": "• Increase in production cost shifts AS curve left.<br></br>• Price level increases.<br></br>• Output decreases."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7apyy97",
      "content": "Graph Axes Explanation:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7qdb5dj",
      "content": "• X-axis → Output (GDP)<br></br>• Y-axis → Price Level<br></br>"
    },
    {
      "id": "eu33ruq",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "RRB HIGH-VALUE EXAM POINTS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tz3t9ng",
      "content": "• Phillips Curve – Short run trade-off exists.<br></br>• Long-run Phillips Curve is vertical.<br></br>• Stagflation = High inflation + High unemployment.<br></br>• Core inflation excludes food &amp; fuel.<br></br>• Demand-pull shifts AD right; Cost-push shifts AS left."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "h7s0avd",
      "content": "• Inflation reduces purchasing power<br></br>• CPI used for inflation targeting<br></br>• Phases: Expansion → Peak → Recession → Depression<br></br>• RBI controls inflation through monetary tools<br></br>"
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
}